#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186197981 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d912b296-6fd0-57c2-84e8-ca0b56549756" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Derivative of a Scalar Function"}] :question/id #uuid "ea202ce3-07d4-5324-9ee4-f5617b430772" :question/math-academy-id "e-12477" :question/problem "For the transformation $f:\\mathbb R^2\\to\\mathbb R,$ defined as\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068404/assets/d8be5d5bd5fa2cd8b618087109678a4f891b08f3788d4946d07bc1b5e4b39a3a.png)\n\ncalculate $\\boldsymbol f'$ at ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068404/assets/a2dbcf34ea50e451efc96ad2f9a7422a7ae507ca8f74088569110abb25293954.png)" :question/worked-solution "Suppose a transformation $\\boldsymbol{f}:\\mathbb R^n\\to\\mathbb R^m$ is defined by \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068404/assets/17588b058b1e1fe934e06679836234f0ef35fe4484a558fcc3ec3b2aafbd2620.png) \n\nwhere $f_1,f_2,\\ldots,f_m$ are scalar functions with $n$ variables. If $\\boldsymbol f$ is differentiable at $\\mathbf{x},$ then the total derivative of $\\boldsymbol f$ at $\\mathbf{x},$ denoted $\\boldsymbol{f}'(\\mathbf{x}),$ is given by the $m \\times n$ matrix\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068404/assets/613ba027e9564812a8e050efd69fd98fff3f614f7d2ec69eeb787c628ccabd12.png)\n\nIn our case, we have the following:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068404/assets/87579b882ca6d8c92d4a7adfed575873fd07c36ab20251722c2cc8fc0f0328e8.png)\n\nFirst, we compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}y)=2xy, & \\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}y)={x}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068404/assets/9fc2431aa874c68b23b6640da987b2f3bc37e2261936f7e1656b04bc3fc0030d.png)\n\nand $\\boldsymbol{f}'$ at ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068404/assets/b83c8f9cb4130103d63821f0d0de50ec0628138dcc8faaf16e8cf9fc27f1a994.png) is\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068404/assets/0851481c21c553b6e0e06a795815b1845e96e0a14f805e440529d0f4d6f85323.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186197982 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6a818e04-786a-56b6-90cf-dcb573ccfa64" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Derivative of a Vector Function"}] :question/id #uuid "ea76d21f-eff8-5634-975f-2b5bd24caf54" :question/math-academy-id "e-12478" :question/problem "For the transformation $\\boldsymbol{f}:\\mathbb R^2\\to\\mathbb R^3,$ defined as\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068404/assets/cf566a0b293a594fa46ae42ec2c4d348d0720b912ef6ef0e333dd3f05f204a9e.png)\n\nthe total derivative $\\boldsymbol f'$ is given by \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068404/assets/5b729806def4b82ee72cd58bc41f39ceb2d1acad82d3a7098fec5bc6be925d6b.png)\nFrom top to bottom, what are the missing entries?" :question/worked-solution "Suppose a transformation $\\boldsymbol{f}:\\mathbb R^n\\to\\mathbb R^m$ is defined by \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068404/assets/0496b786dfda2338d951906d6fafb261e9aee95d9390423e69a5a55a76790918.png) \n\nwhere $f_1,f_2,\\ldots,f_m$ are scalar functions with $n$ variables. If $\\boldsymbol{f}$ is differentiable at $\\mathbf{x},$ then the total derivative of $\\boldsymbol{f}$ at $\\mathbf{x},$ denoted $\\boldsymbol{f}'(\\mathbf{x}),$ is given by the $m \\times n$ matrix\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068404/assets/bb37d8fdb7e4da90a22933c264d49ff999a3502618a6cd3725e8a5a2fd55a9ed.png)\n\nIn our case, we have the following:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068404/assets/f2c5b815b56c791d1538c225c954c2fdc5603f879e4254838bb73994b6493d48.png)\n\nFirst, we compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(xy)=y,\\, & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(xy)=x, \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({y}^{2})=0,\\, & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({y}^{2})=2y, \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{3}}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(y\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)=\\frac{y}{x},\\, & \\frac{∂{f}_{3}}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(y\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068404/assets/238be519e096397dafb2ad5b915d07a09f5129dc897b45955715e76da1146d1e.png)\nThus, the missing entries are $y,\\:$ $0,\\:$ and $\\ln{x}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186197983 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0e90349c-33ae-5b60-9d0d-7542dfebbbc7" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Tangent Plane to the Graph of a Scalar Function in Matrix Form"}] :question/id #uuid "db0be438-94fe-52de-9daf-60d1727ce7b9" :question/math-academy-id "e-12479" :question/problem "Consider the function $f:\\mathbb R^2\\to\\mathbb R,$ defined as\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068404/assets/f11de75b045b391687224fe118c2e1d3ec6d22e476ed030a3af10b55afb63eae.png)\n\nIf the tangent to $f$ at ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068404/assets/11c6c7d42c15626ed4a04d31dabbb6a9dea649c25240c350c46eae80ea55f687.png) is given by\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068404/assets/890997aca384f6846dda8a9465aa36a838f76d3db05eca1dbc7725cc03413599.png)\n\nfind the missing values." :question/worked-solution "Suppose a transformation $\\boldsymbol{f}:\\mathbb R^n\\to\\mathbb R^m$ is defined by \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068404/assets/f18ed650b92e1d02e809d5eb997a231ec9a118da285292f88339bb4fdc3aaf95.png) \n\nwhere $f_1,f_2,\\ldots,f_m$ are scalar functions with $n$ variables. If $\\boldsymbol{f}$ is differentiable at $\\mathbf{x},$ then the total derivative of $\\boldsymbol{f}$ at $\\mathbf{x},$ denoted $\\boldsymbol{f}'(\\mathbf{x}),$ is given by the $m \\times n$ matrix\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068404/assets/613ba027e9564812a8e050efd69fd98fff3f614f7d2ec69eeb787c628ccabd12.png)\n\nIn our case, we have the following:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068404/assets/87579b882ca6d8c92d4a7adfed575873fd07c36ab20251722c2cc8fc0f0328e8.png)\n\nFirst, we compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{3}+{e}^{y})=3{x}^{2},\\, & \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{3}+{e}^{y})={e}^{y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068404/assets/dcff4801886965e64a2e145869bd8c1ee4559c8cbe458661d53ad06ecd6ddb30.png)\n\nEvaluating $f$ and its derivative at ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068404/assets/e73720f8e1c08238a11ab557a3e515a214b3b9ed76000ca900ccf801de5d76c4.png) we have\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068404/assets/6d7d1453ae6acad9a4d99359bcf40f4e90ac3383ade8a0aff58c82097fe37fde.png)\n\nThe tangent to $f$ at $\\mathbf x = \\mathbf a$ is given by\n\n$$\nz - f(\\mathbf a) = \\boldsymbol{f}'(\\mathbf a)(\\mathbf x - \\mathbf a).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $f(\\mathbf a),$ $\\boldsymbol{f}'(\\mathbf a),$ and $\\mathbf a$ in the equation above, we obtain\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068404/assets/5c360a03ebca35811d9d95508cf4dc08481865040c64aa6f608202de88af98f2.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186197984 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9f09fc28-bdce-554f-98f5-019d34542a13" :knowledge-point/title "Finding an Affine Approximation of a Vector Function"}] :question/id #uuid "f3540571-9159-50b4-a46c-4cf28a454602" :question/math-academy-id "e-12484" :question/problem "Consider the transformation $\\boldsymbol{f}:\\mathbb R^2\\to\\mathbb R^2,$ defined as\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068404/assets/be3163cd89092fe54a0349a901b6bbd36829c265f1a1fc51493b8a992b8c13d1.png)\n\nIf the linear approximation of $\\boldsymbol f$ at ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068404/assets/4043ac6ae5b5e2664350b31956c1c75f6d2441e5f2d48a284e3e5340e4824de4.png) is given by\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068404/assets/04e15d28c62e16e51f6cf3eb5d7d2e84a5ac7f0bdf3b65e9d1e5f5baf71eb590.png)\n\nwhat are the missing values?" :question/worked-solution "Suppose a transformation $\\boldsymbol{f}:\\mathbb R^n\\to\\mathbb R^m$ is defined by \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068404/assets/e79145a13ada389ac337a69f8c48952f53b70d5caf48d950b305275ed8773b44.png) \n\nwhere $f_1,f_2,\\ldots,f_m$ are scalar functions with $n$ variables. If $\\boldsymbol{f}$ is differentiable at $\\mathbf{x},$ then the total derivative of $\\boldsymbol{f}$ at $\\mathbf{x},$ denoted $\\boldsymbol{f}'(\\mathbf{x}),$ is given by the $m \\times n$ matrix\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068404/assets/5366c8bcd23e435ac2ecb0dc523f8a828583486a46a246a92abf4762fc55e789.png)\n\nIn our case, we have the following:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068404/assets/7bd197f9a502e48966fc902bba2d0fe8b8ddd3a0ce767d80b7a68b2a53a0aebb.png)\n\nFirst, we compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{1}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{1}}({x}_{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡{x}_{1})={x}_{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{x}_{1},\\, & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{2}}({x}_{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡{x}_{1})=\\operatorname{sin}⁡{x}_{1} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{1}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{1}}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡{x}_{2})=0,\\, & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{2}}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡{x}_{2})=\\operatorname{cos}⁡{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068404/assets/7b54f254580d3374c6535d0935f1ba8e4a7d5ca4eca0aab424900097dd217684.png)\n\nEvaluating $\\boldsymbol{f}$ and its derivative at ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068404/assets/22f4d34b8ec830740b285e1c31954b1e382264c4f366d3ea426ecadd3fd5f5bb.png) we have\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068404/assets/651b14a10334bdfc073b86359ce306c1b4ba25b9390f345b609978e34cc08cad.png)\n\nThe linear approximation of $\\boldsymbol{f}$ at $\\mathbf x = \\mathbf a$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\boldsymbol{f}\\left(\\mathbf x \\right) \\approx \\boldsymbol{f}(\\mathbf a) + \\boldsymbol{f}'(\\mathbf a)(\\mathbf x - \\mathbf a).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $\\boldsymbol{f}(\\mathbf a),$ $\\boldsymbol{f}'(\\mathbf a),$ and $\\mathbf a$ in the equation above, we obtain\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068404/assets/3faf4b27b2df75a32661fb97309ee83c4d7bbd906729702119cba79bbf06b1f6.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198559 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6a818e04-786a-56b6-90cf-dcb573ccfa64" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Derivative of a Vector Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "84a02a54-5df2-54f3-bf70-6fa9b47be689" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2y \\\\ ye^{xy}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194256} {:answer/id #uuid "aba6b2d2-aff8-59c9-9848-36111e68c66c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}ye^{xy} & 2x \\\\ 2y & xe^{xy}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194257} {:answer/id #uuid "efa88cd6-7e18-5c6a-8ca8-e8ec1ddd543c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2x \\\\ xe^{xy}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194258} {:answer/id #uuid "50267c0b-dd49-55b6-88d9-96cb362c6ddb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2y & 2x \\\\ ye^{xy} & xe^{xy}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194259} {:answer/id #uuid "7d6d9c79-2d49-5e22-9cba-3a8eec112f6e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2xy & 2xy \\\\ e^{xy} & e^{xy}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194260}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "50267c0b-dd49-55b6-88d9-96cb362c6ddb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2y & 2x \\\\ ye^{xy} & xe^{xy}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194259} :answer-field/id #uuid "a73dc2d2-ecde-5655-8b25-96066ebce803" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194255}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "fcfc99a4-cdcc-57b4-bd0a-78e0c8273abc" :question/math-academy-id "q-162941" :question/problem "For the transformation $f:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2},$ defined as\n\n$$\nf(x)=[\\begin{aligned}2xy \\\\ {e}^{xy}\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\ncalculate ${f}^{′}(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose a transformation $f:{R}^{n}\\to {R}^{m}$ is defined by \n\n$$\nf:[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}{f}_{1}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}) \\\\ {f}_{2}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}) \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {f}_{m}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n})\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere ${f}_{1},{f}_{2},…,{f}_{m}$ are scalar functions with $n$ variables. If $f$ is differentiable at $x,$ then the total derivative of $f$ at $x,$ denoted ${f}^{′}(x),$ is given by the $m\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{n}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have the following:\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂x} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂y} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂x} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂y}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2xy)=2y,\\, & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2xy)=2x \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({e}^{xy})=y{e}^{xy},\\, & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({e}^{xy})=x{e}^{xy}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}2y & 2x \\\\ y{e}^{xy} & x{e}^{xy}\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198562 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9f09fc28-bdce-554f-98f5-019d34542a13" :knowledge-point/title "Finding an Affine Approximation of a Vector Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a70874ed-0a2c-5282-9cfa-59d9ab860d6a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194274} {:answer/id #uuid "2d7b9d3e-784c-586a-9879-40767c031372" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\ln 2 + 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194275} {:answer/id #uuid "435041c2-14bc-582b-b3f6-92f84da5d38d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194276} {:answer/id #uuid "7118024b-0a04-596a-9f19-b38afdb111fb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\ln 2 + 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194277} {:answer/id #uuid "7cc45380-684f-589e-8c7f-a99f1c78da7b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\ln 2 + 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194278}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2d7b9d3e-784c-586a-9879-40767c031372" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\ln 2 + 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194275} :answer-field/id #uuid "e8aeb739-36a3-5843-95b5-cde0db730ec5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194273}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "e8bf8960-3077-5130-9de0-3e5c9b2bef5d" :question/math-academy-id "q-162944" :question/problem "Consider the transformation $f:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2},$ defined as\n\n$$\nf(x)=[\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}{x}_{2} \\\\ {e}^{{x}_{1}{x}_{2}}\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf the linear approximation of $f$ at $a=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\end{aligned}]$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)≈[\\begin{aligned}∗ \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2 & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & 2\\end{aligned}](x-[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\end{aligned}]),\n$$\n\nwhat is the sum of the missing values?" :question/worked-solution "Suppose a transformation $f:{R}^{n}\\to {R}^{m}$ is defined by \n\n$$\nf:[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}{f}_{1}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}) \\\\ {f}_{2}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}) \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {f}_{m}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n})\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere ${f}_{1},{f}_{2},…,{f}_{m}$ are scalar functions with $n$ variables. If $f$ is differentiable at $x,$ then the total derivative of $f$ at $x,$ denoted ${f}^{′}(x),$ is given by the $m\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{n}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have the following:\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{2}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{2}}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{1}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{1}}(2{x}_{1}{x}_{2})=2{x}_{2},\\, & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{2}}(2{x}_{1}{x}_{2})=2{x}_{1} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{1}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{1}}({e}^{{x}_{1}{x}_{2}})={x}_{2}{e}^{{x}_{1}{x}_{2}},\\, & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{2}}({e}^{{x}_{1}{x}_{2}})={x}_{1}{e}^{{x}_{1}{x}_{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{2} & 2{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}{e}^{{x}_{1}{x}_{2}} & {x}_{1}{e}^{{x}_{1}{x}_{2}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nEvaluating $f$ and its derivative at $x=a=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\end{aligned}],$ we have\n\n$$\nf(a)=[\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,{f}^{′}(a)=[\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2 & 2 \\\\ 2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe linear approximation of $f$ at $x=a$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)≈f(a)+{f}^{′}(a)(x-a).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $f(a),$ ${f}^{′}(a),$ and $a$ in the equation above, we obtain\n\n$$\nf(x)≈[\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2 & 2 \\\\ 2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2 & 2\\end{aligned}](x-[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\end{aligned}]).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the sum of the missing values is\n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2+2=4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2+2.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186363558 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d912b296-6fd0-57c2-84e8-ca0b56549756" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Derivative of a Scalar Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a2a467d-9bdf-5ae9-bb27-429636af45a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2} & -{y}^{2}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363560} {:answer/id #uuid "66f3281d-1cc3-5707-be84-675eefaab8a8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2x \\\\ -3y\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363561} {:answer/id #uuid "3434148b-a4e4-5d15-83bd-cc1ed32bdc60" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}6y \\\\ -4x\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363562} {:answer/id #uuid "87eb1930-6b43-53c3-8812-9caa11ee4a1d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4x & -6y\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363563} {:answer/id #uuid "8c4622c0-cca7-5d8b-8e19-8d33517e1d97" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 & -6\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363564}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "87eb1930-6b43-53c3-8812-9caa11ee4a1d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4x & -6y\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363563} :answer-field/id #uuid "ceadf31d-0ba7-5c2c-91c5-a0b3650e8da5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363559}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "64d550f1-8d2f-5aa7-8e7b-a4c907c4afdf" :question/math-academy-id "q-163032" :question/problem "For the function $f:{R}^{2}\\to R,$ defined as\n\n$$\nf(x)=2{x}^{2}-3{y}^{2},\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\ncalculate ${f}^{′}(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose a transformation $f:{R}^{n}\\to {R}^{m}$ is defined by \n\n$$\nf:[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}{f}_{1}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}) \\\\ {f}_{2}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}) \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {f}_{m}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n})\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere ${f}_{1},{f}_{2},…,{f}_{m}$ are scalar functions with $n$ variables. If $f$ is differentiable at $x,$ then the total derivative of $f$ at $x,$ denoted ${f}^{′}(x),$ is given by the $m\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{n}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have the following:\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & \\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2{x}^{2}-3{y}^{2})=4x, & \\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2{x}^{2}-3{y}^{2})=-6y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}4x & -6y\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186363565 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d912b296-6fd0-57c2-84e8-ca0b56549756" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Derivative of a Scalar Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "47e7e965-734e-5221-88fd-9fe717b12fb2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363567} {:answer/id #uuid "15291af6-91a5-5f2a-8f54-787f16abd300" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y & x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363568} {:answer/id #uuid "1b71bd6e-8740-5c04-b466-37ec003f65ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y & x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363569} {:answer/id #uuid "441a4d54-6bcf-55a6-8be9-30d8c0609b93" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y & x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363570} {:answer/id #uuid "6031cf86-6595-5340-a0c5-2fca285b402f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363571}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "441a4d54-6bcf-55a6-8be9-30d8c0609b93" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y & x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363570} :answer-field/id #uuid "4ee5b226-ce63-53cf-9491-061afa62b434" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363566}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "481039ec-e171-5d00-9cb6-0349111018af" :question/math-academy-id "q-163033" :question/problem "For the function $f:{R}^{2}\\to R,$ defined as\n\n$$\nf(x)=x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y,\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\ncalculate ${f}^{′}(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose a transformation $f:{R}^{n}\\to {R}^{m}$ is defined by \n\n$$\nf:[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}{f}_{1}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}) \\\\ {f}_{2}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}) \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {f}_{m}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n})\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere ${f}_{1},{f}_{2},…,{f}_{m}$ are scalar functions with $n$ variables. If $f$ is differentiable at $x,$ then the total derivative of $f$ at $x,$ denoted ${f}^{′}(x),$ is given by the $m\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{n}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have the following:\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & \\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡y, & \\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y)=x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y & x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186363572 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d912b296-6fd0-57c2-84e8-ca0b56549756" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Derivative of a Scalar Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6e55cb00-638f-520a-8498-b89993f51aeb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363574} {:answer/id #uuid "e783d05f-2fc3-5115-8661-58844887006c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 & 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363575} {:answer/id #uuid "b739c1d3-7ece-5955-8447-27b166d2513f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}12 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363576} {:answer/id #uuid "c2d9c58e-af98-5368-8b7d-91f69e3d20e6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 12\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363577} {:answer/id #uuid "f92d586a-84e1-55f9-b37b-df2b977fd1d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363578}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e783d05f-2fc3-5115-8661-58844887006c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 & 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363575} :answer-field/id #uuid "37273e20-c281-533a-8df9-7bd71e25382b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363573}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "86347eb1-d7e8-5d5a-b478-0a57c42a6dd9" :question/math-academy-id "q-163044" :question/problem "For the transformation $f:{R}^{2}\\to R,$ defined as\n\n$$\nf(x)={x}^{2}+{y}^{3},\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\ncalculate ${f}^{′}$ at $a=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose a transformation $f:{R}^{n}\\to {R}^{m}$ is defined by \n\n$$\nf:[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}{f}_{1}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}) \\\\ {f}_{2}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}) \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {f}_{m}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n})\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere ${f}_{1},{f}_{2},…,{f}_{m}$ are scalar functions with $n$ variables. If $f$ is differentiable at $x,$ then the total derivative of $f$ at $x,$ denoted ${f}^{′}(x),$ is given by the $m\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{n}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have the following:\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & \\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}+{y}^{3})=2x, & \\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}+{y}^{3})=3{y}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}2x & 3{y}^{2}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nand ${f}^{′}$ at $a=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ is\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(a)=[\\begin{aligned}2(2) & 3(1)^{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186363579 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d912b296-6fd0-57c2-84e8-ca0b56549756" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Derivative of a Scalar Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3020d3aa-975b-5ed5-84e2-550e19e6e186" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363581} {:answer/id #uuid "7f88a80a-1e86-5c0f-a77a-528bb6847cc6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363582} {:answer/id #uuid "07ddfe91-b929-5d44-8cc8-25b095a32bb8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363583} {:answer/id #uuid "34ae9f66-f2e8-59ca-b5f7-09163398e965" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363584} {:answer/id #uuid "808757ec-fd8a-5720-ae12-375472fd5452" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363585}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "808757ec-fd8a-5720-ae12-375472fd5452" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363585} :answer-field/id #uuid "c1c7b816-258e-5d1f-b7f9-0bf373101c4a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363580}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2b3bff85-1a01-5938-a4f3-da66675bd3b2" :question/math-academy-id "q-163046" :question/problem "For the transformation $f:{R}^{2}\\to R,$ defined as\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{x}{y},\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\ncalculate ${f}^{′}$ at $a=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose a transformation $f:{R}^{n}\\to {R}^{m}$ is defined by \n\n$$\nf:[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}{f}_{1}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}) \\\\ {f}_{2}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}) \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {f}_{m}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n})\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere ${f}_{1},{f}_{2},…,{f}_{m}$ are scalar functions with $n$ variables. If $f$ is differentiable at $x,$ then the total derivative of $f$ at $x,$ denoted ${f}^{′}(x),$ is given by the $m\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{n}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have the following:\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & \\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{x}{y})=\\frac{1}{y}, & \\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\frac{x}{y})=-\\frac{x}{{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{y} & -\\frac{x}{{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nand ${f}^{′}$ at $a=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ is\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(a)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{(1)} & -\\frac{(-2)}{(1)^{2}}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186363586 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d912b296-6fd0-57c2-84e8-ca0b56549756" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Derivative of a Scalar Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "53e19843-4697-59df-a7e4-246b12d665f9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2x & 3{y}^{2}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363588} {:answer/id #uuid "c9520b30-e0ac-58b9-877d-bfa29d26703c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}xy & {x}^{2}{y}^{2}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363589} {:answer/id #uuid "9b44b44a-fc5d-5752-befa-dd0f73538bbc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2x{y}^{3} & 2{x}^{2}{y}^{2}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363590} {:answer/id #uuid "79ad81c7-a983-5c6c-9746-831542259cd7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2x{y}^{3} & 3{x}^{2}{y}^{2}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363591} {:answer/id #uuid "db9eeb3e-14be-5d2f-8e1f-68fc5258aca8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2xy & 3xy\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363592}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "79ad81c7-a983-5c6c-9746-831542259cd7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2x{y}^{3} & 3{x}^{2}{y}^{2}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363591} :answer-field/id #uuid "b62a4d41-30d8-528d-afaa-712e3df6d786" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363587}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ee96e632-e895-5789-9355-766910a251b7" :question/math-academy-id "q-163047" :question/problem "For the function $f:{R}^{2}\\to R,$ defined as\n\n$$\nf(x)={x}^{2}{y}^{3},\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\ncalculate ${f}^{′}(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose a transformation $f:{R}^{n}\\to {R}^{m}$ is defined by \n\n$$\nf:[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}{f}_{1}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}) \\\\ {f}_{2}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}) \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {f}_{m}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n})\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere ${f}_{1},{f}_{2},…,{f}_{m}$ are scalar functions with $n$ variables. If $f$ is differentiable at $x,$ then the total derivative of $f$ at $x,$ denoted ${f}^{′}(x),$ is given by the $m\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{n}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have the following:\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & \\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}{y}^{3})=2x{y}^{3}, & \\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}{y}^{3})=3{x}^{2}{y}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}2x{y}^{3} & 3{x}^{2}{y}^{2}\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186363593 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0e90349c-33ae-5b60-9d0d-7542dfebbbc7" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Tangent Plane to the Graph of a Scalar Function in Matrix Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ab7f96d1-e25a-58f2-abac-a391e964f889" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363595} {:answer/id #uuid "4acb09ad-7e95-5421-8566-28fa5a62e51b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363596} {:answer/id #uuid "ef2c10bd-dbaf-50fb-b8a5-9e39a59de7a9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363597} {:answer/id #uuid "cc12a0fe-6b1a-5189-a97e-08d47f51a53a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363598} {:answer/id #uuid "488a23d9-e996-5853-9b60-a26335a3fb26" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363599}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ef2c10bd-dbaf-50fb-b8a5-9e39a59de7a9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363597} :answer-field/id #uuid "1675867a-833a-5ac7-8580-3880817458ee" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363594}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "364bef26-7750-5429-8f55-8f969b2c35ec" :question/math-academy-id "q-163056" :question/problem "Consider the function $f:{R}^{2}\\to R,$ defined as\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy),\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf the tangent to $f$ at $a=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ \\pi \\end{aligned}]$ is given by\n\n$$\nz-∗=[\\begin{aligned}∗ & ∗\\end{aligned}]([\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ \\pi \\end{aligned}])\n$$\n\nwhat is the sum of the missing values?" :question/worked-solution "Suppose a transformation $f:{R}^{n}\\to {R}^{m}$ is defined by \n\n$$\nf:[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}{f}_{1}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}) \\\\ {f}_{2}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}) \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {f}_{m}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n})\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere ${f}_{1},{f}_{2},…,{f}_{m}$ are scalar functions with $n$ variables. If $f$ is differentiable at $x,$ then the total derivative of $f$ at $x,$ denoted ${f}^{′}(x),$ is given by the $m\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{n}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have the following:\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & \\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy))=y\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy),\\, & \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy))=x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}y\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy) & x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nEvaluating $f$ and its derivative at $x=a=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ \\pi \\end{aligned}],$ we have\n\n$$\nf(a)=0,\\,{f}^{′}(a)=[\\begin{aligned}\\pi  & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe tangent to $f$ at $x=a$ is given by\n\n$$\nz-f(a)={f}^{′}(a)(x-a).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $f(a),$ ${f}^{′}(a),$ and $a$ in the equation above, we obtain\n\n$$\nz-0=[\\begin{aligned}\\pi  & 0\\end{aligned}]([\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ \\pi \\end{aligned}]).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the sum of the missing values is\n\n$$\n0+\\pi +0=\\pi .\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186363600 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0e90349c-33ae-5b60-9d0d-7542dfebbbc7" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Tangent Plane to the Graph of a Scalar Function in Matrix Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ba8ae65-d975-5af0-96d5-26620fb73ec3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3e-2}{e}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363602} {:answer/id #uuid "5d8917aa-77f7-54ff-b8e0-253a68794c6f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4e+1}{e}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363603} {:answer/id #uuid "c7f1d8da-1683-542e-8149-4d71b7fe1f4d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3e+4}{e}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363604} {:answer/id #uuid "39b7be7d-65bf-5460-8a27-1f69998b7f45" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5e+2}{e}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363605} {:answer/id #uuid "0223940f-90bf-5112-91b4-b372b333d359" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4e-1}{e}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363606}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5d8917aa-77f7-54ff-b8e0-253a68794c6f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4e+1}{e}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363603} :answer-field/id #uuid "4d98f419-eab8-54bf-a1e2-ac16387d8dc7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363601}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "bbe7433e-c5fe-50b2-9856-fe34362f2673" :question/math-academy-id "q-163058" :question/problem "Consider the function $f:{R}^{2}\\to R,$ defined as\n\n$$\nf(x)={x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡y,\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf the tangent to $f$ at $a=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ e\\end{aligned}]$ is given by\n\n$$\nz-∗=[\\begin{aligned}∗ & ∗\\end{aligned}]([\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ e\\end{aligned}])\n$$\n\nwhat is the sum of the missing values?" :question/worked-solution "Suppose a transformation $f:{R}^{n}\\to {R}^{m}$ is defined by \n\n$$\nf:[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}{f}_{1}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}) \\\\ {f}_{2}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}) \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {f}_{m}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n})\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere ${f}_{1},{f}_{2},…,{f}_{m}$ are scalar functions with $n$ variables. If $f$ is differentiable at $x,$ then the total derivative of $f$ at $x,$ denoted ${f}^{′}(x),$ is given by the $m\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{n}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have the following:\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & \\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡y)=3{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡y,\\, & \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡y)=\\frac{{x}^{3}}{y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}3{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡y & \\frac{{x}^{3}}{y}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nEvaluating $f$ and its derivative at $x=a=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ e\\end{aligned}],$ we have\n\n$$\nf(a)=1,\\,{f}^{′}(a)=[\\begin{aligned}3 & \\frac{1}{e}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe tangent to $f$ at $x=a$ is given by\n\n$$\nz-f(a)={f}^{′}(a)(x-a).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $f(a),$ ${f}^{′}(a),$ and $a$ in the equation above, we obtain\n\n$$\nz-1=[\\begin{aligned}3 & \\frac{1}{e}\\end{aligned}]([\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ e\\end{aligned}]).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the sum of the missing values is\n\n$$\n1+3+\\frac{1}{e}=\\frac{4e+1}{e}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186363607 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0e90349c-33ae-5b60-9d0d-7542dfebbbc7" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Tangent Plane to the Graph of a Scalar Function in Matrix Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8bbce4e2-f350-5dca-bdd1-7abbe4dd8d9f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363609} {:answer/id #uuid "76fcca6f-5297-5be9-8895-6e0f5ac7aba7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2+\\frac{\\pi }{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363610} {:answer/id #uuid "ae29e439-fae1-529b-b39d-151288811af0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363611} {:answer/id #uuid "761f45f6-c661-561f-bb69-ba4b618f63b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363612} {:answer/id #uuid "d23856d0-cc6d-57ba-8ad5-96de0beb45f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363613}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "761f45f6-c661-561f-bb69-ba4b618f63b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363612} :answer-field/id #uuid "52a4d14f-4501-5604-b1e6-cb82a74ecf6f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363608}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "184e02f8-9497-5f94-828d-a4dd30e0b39d" :question/math-academy-id "q-163075" :question/problem "Consider the function $f:{R}^{2}\\to R,$ defined as\n\n$$\nf(x)=y\\operatorname{tan}⁡x,\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf the tangent to $f$ at $a=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\pi }{4} \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$ is given by\n\n$$\nz-∗=[\\begin{aligned}∗ & ∗\\end{aligned}]([\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\pi }{4} \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}])\n$$\n\nwhat is the sum of the missing values?" :question/worked-solution "Suppose a transformation $f:{R}^{n}\\to {R}^{m}$ is defined by \n\n$$\nf:[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}{f}_{1}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}) \\\\ {f}_{2}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}) \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {f}_{m}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n})\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere ${f}_{1},{f}_{2},…,{f}_{m}$ are scalar functions with $n$ variables. If $f$ is differentiable at $x,$ then the total derivative of $f$ at $x,$ denoted ${f}^{′}(x),$ is given by the $m\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{n}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have the following:\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & \\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(y\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)=\\frac{y}{{cos}^{2}⁡x},\\, & \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(y\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{y}{{cos}^{2}⁡x} & \\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nEvaluating $f$ and its derivative at $x=a=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\pi }{4} \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],$ we have\n\n$$\nf(a)=2,\\,{f}^{′}(a)=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe tangent to $f$ at $x=a$ is given by\n\n$$\nz-f(a)={f}^{′}(a)(x-a).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $f(a),$ ${f}^{′}(a),$ and $a$ in the equation above, we obtain\n\n$$\nz-2=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 1\\end{aligned}]([\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\pi }{4} \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the sum of the missing values is\n\n$$\n2+4+1=7.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186363614 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0e90349c-33ae-5b60-9d0d-7542dfebbbc7" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Tangent Plane to the Graph of a Scalar Function in Matrix Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "51cd2c35-18ce-5199-ba6f-165a0c05005d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5{e}^{2}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363616} {:answer/id #uuid "beab36ea-6740-52ff-943a-8b65ef61c0f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7{e}^{2}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363617} {:answer/id #uuid "d7d6a33f-a487-58b9-a9cb-14a8a552ea3f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3{e}^{2}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363618} {:answer/id #uuid "3a434b9b-b217-57c5-bc28-c02328bc35fc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7{e}^{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363619} {:answer/id #uuid "7b83f53a-bfe9-5fca-a9d6-2edfd9f4b84e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363620}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "51cd2c35-18ce-5199-ba6f-165a0c05005d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5{e}^{2}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363616} :answer-field/id #uuid "fdf10705-4f15-5698-a7fd-41478a30867b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363615}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "97408f05-561b-583e-b4ea-54fdcf90e2e0" :question/math-academy-id "q-163076" :question/problem "Consider the function $f:{R}^{2}\\to R,$ defined as\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{{e}^{2x}}{y},\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf the tangent to $f$ at $a=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$ is given by\n\n$$\nz-∗=[\\begin{aligned}∗ & ∗\\end{aligned}]([\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}])\n$$\n\nwhat is the sum of the missing values?" :question/worked-solution "Suppose a transformation $f:{R}^{n}\\to {R}^{m}$ is defined by \n\n$$\nf:[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}{f}_{1}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}) \\\\ {f}_{2}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}) \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {f}_{m}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n})\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere ${f}_{1},{f}_{2},…,{f}_{m}$ are scalar functions with $n$ variables. If $f$ is differentiable at $x,$ then the total derivative of $f$ at $x,$ denoted ${f}^{′}(x),$ is given by the $m\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{n}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have the following:\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & \\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{{e}^{2x}}{y})=\\frac{2{e}^{2x}}{y},\\, & \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\frac{{e}^{2x}}{y})=-\\frac{{e}^{2x}}{{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2{e}^{2x}}{y} & -\\frac{{e}^{2x}}{{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nEvaluating $f$ and its derivative at $x=a=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],$ we have\n\n$$\nf(a)=\\frac{{e}^{2}}{2},\\,{f}^{′}(a)=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2} & -\\frac{{e}^{2}}{4}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe tangent to $f$ at $x=a$ is given by\n\n$$\nz-f(a)={f}^{′}(a)(x-a).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $f(a),$ ${f}^{′}(a),$ and $a$ in the equation above, we obtain\n\n$$\nz-\\frac{{e}^{2}}{2}=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2} & -\\frac{{e}^{2}}{4}\\end{aligned}]([\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the sum of the missing values is\n\n$$\n\\frac{{e}^{2}}{2}+{e}^{2}+(-\\frac{{e}^{2}}{4})=\\frac{5{e}^{2}}{4}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186363621 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0e90349c-33ae-5b60-9d0d-7542dfebbbc7" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Tangent Plane to the Graph of a Scalar Function in Matrix Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "acf6e627-64e7-59cc-8ff8-90f5198de906" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363623} {:answer/id #uuid "90521cb4-ee70-50f7-bdde-8b1f58858204" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363624} {:answer/id #uuid "b0fd40e9-5f34-542d-ac48-c62e4cc148ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363625} {:answer/id #uuid "7f80ec90-e9a0-5638-aeea-ca7f7fd1dd89" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363626} {:answer/id #uuid "b416a8ca-9ac6-54a2-922e-d36c8db1d094" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363627}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b0fd40e9-5f34-542d-ac48-c62e4cc148ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363625} :answer-field/id #uuid "5a1eb086-f11d-55c3-be2e-f7d8cfe68697" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363622}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "aec3f0d4-dfe4-5092-884c-654f878a0c93" :question/math-academy-id "q-163078" :question/problem "Consider the function $f:{R}^{2}\\to R,$ defined as\n\n$$\nf(x)={x}^{2}+xy,\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf the tangent to $f$ at $a=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ is given by\n\n$$\nz-∗=[\\begin{aligned}∗ & ∗\\end{aligned}]([\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}])\n$$\n\nwhat is the sum of the missing values?" :question/worked-solution "Suppose a transformation $f:{R}^{n}\\to {R}^{m}$ is defined by \n\n$$\nf:[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}{f}_{1}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}) \\\\ {f}_{2}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}) \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {f}_{m}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n})\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere ${f}_{1},{f}_{2},…,{f}_{m}$ are scalar functions with $n$ variables. If $f$ is differentiable at $x,$ then the total derivative of $f$ at $x,$ denoted ${f}^{′}(x),$ is given by the $m\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{n}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have the following:\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & \\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}+xy)=2x+y,\\, & \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}+xy)=x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}2x+y & x\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nEvaluating $f$ and its derivative at $x=a=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],$ we have\n\n$$\nf(a)=2,\\,{f}^{′}(a)=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe tangent to $f$ at $x=a$ is given by\n\n$$\nz-f(a)={f}^{′}(a)(x-a).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $f(a),$ ${f}^{′}(a),$ and $a$ in the equation above, we obtain\n\n$$\nz-2=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -2\\end{aligned}]([\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the sum of the missing values is\n\n$$\n2+(-3)+(-2)=-3.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186363628 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9f09fc28-bdce-554f-98f5-019d34542a13" :knowledge-point/title "Finding an Affine Approximation of a Vector Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ea6aa0ef-7827-5bc9-8685-800a4d5ebb6c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363630} {:answer/id #uuid "50a46d89-bfb7-5b3c-83c4-25c4cb9a84a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363631} {:answer/id #uuid "3b7e11fa-11b2-59e1-8954-052354500304" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363632} {:answer/id #uuid "9c18b2c2-4ab2-522f-85d8-40c838846109" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363633} {:answer/id #uuid "daaf09e6-ab01-5583-8cba-0a2fd9a25407" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363634}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "daaf09e6-ab01-5583-8cba-0a2fd9a25407" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363634} :answer-field/id #uuid "1b99d46a-57ce-5f0b-8e97-0167b64a7490" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363629}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "783dd4bf-2bc5-51d9-add7-0b01d999695d" :question/math-academy-id "q-163091" :question/problem "Consider the transformation $f:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2},$ defined as\n\n$$\nf(x)=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2}{e}^{{x}_{1}} \\\\ 3{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf the linear approximation of $f$ at  $a=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)≈[\\begin{aligned}∗ \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & 2\\end{aligned}](x-[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]),\n$$\n\nwhat is the sum of the missing values?" :question/worked-solution "Suppose a transformation $f:{R}^{n}\\to {R}^{m}$ is defined by \n\n$$\nf:[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}{f}_{1}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}) \\\\ {f}_{2}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}) \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {f}_{m}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n})\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere ${f}_{1},{f}_{2},…,{f}_{m}$ are scalar functions with $n$ variables. If $f$ is differentiable at $x,$ then the total derivative of $f$ at $x,$ denoted ${f}^{′}(x),$ is given by the $m\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{n}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have the following:\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{2}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{2}}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{1}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{1}}({x}_{2}{e}^{{x}_{1}})={x}_{2}{e}^{{x}_{1}},\\, & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{2}}({x}_{2}{e}^{{x}_{1}})={e}^{{x}_{1}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{1}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{1}}(3{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2})=3,\\, & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{2}}(3{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2})=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2}{e}^{{x}_{1}} & {e}^{{x}_{1}} \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nEvaluating $f$ and its derivative at $x=a=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],$ we have\n\n$$\nf(a)=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,{f}^{′}(a)=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe linear approximation of $f$ at $x=a$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)≈f(a)+{f}^{′}(a)(x-a).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $f(a),$ ${f}^{′}(a),$ and $a$ in the equation above, we obtain\n\n$$\nf(x)≈[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{aligned}](x-[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the sum of the missing values is\n\n$$\n1+1+3=5.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186363635 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9f09fc28-bdce-554f-98f5-019d34542a13" :knowledge-point/title "Finding an Affine Approximation of a Vector Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7bed27a4-8e04-573d-a5b0-50c65860183f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{e}^{-1}-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363637} {:answer/id #uuid "1cd3a9ee-96dd-5642-a004-fd6b80f0bb12" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-1}-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363638} {:answer/id #uuid "51bda9ab-514d-5355-8273-558947208187" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{e}^{-1}+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363639} {:answer/id #uuid "163d1b16-1780-5e77-8a8d-58a43a98be84" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363640} {:answer/id #uuid "81f50bdc-901e-50e9-b995-a62c062a6ba0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-1}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363641}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1cd3a9ee-96dd-5642-a004-fd6b80f0bb12" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-1}-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363638} :answer-field/id #uuid "56fadb67-7c11-536e-8f87-2639d82d3ca7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363636}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "e5559282-4ede-5e15-818d-c78fa2d94593" :question/math-academy-id "q-163093" :question/problem "Consider the transformation $f:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2},$ defined as\n\n$$\nf(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}_{1})+{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}^{2}+1\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf the linear approximation of $f$ at  $a=[\\begin{aligned}e \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)≈[\\begin{aligned}∗ \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}∗ & 1 \\\\ 0 & ∗\\end{aligned}](x-[\\begin{aligned}e \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]),\n$$\n\nwhat is the sum of the missing values?" :question/worked-solution "Suppose a transformation $f:{R}^{n}\\to {R}^{m}$ is defined by \n\n$$\nf:[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}{f}_{1}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}) \\\\ {f}_{2}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}) \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {f}_{m}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n})\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere ${f}_{1},{f}_{2},…,{f}_{m}$ are scalar functions with $n$ variables. If $f$ is differentiable at $x,$ then the total derivative of $f$ at $x,$ denoted ${f}^{′}(x),$ is given by the $m\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{n}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have the following:\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{2}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{2}}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{1}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{1}}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}_{1})+{x}_{2})=\\frac{1}{{x}_{1}},\\, & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{2}}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}_{1})+{x}_{2})=1 \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{1}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{1}}({x}_{2}^{2}+1)=0,\\, & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{2}}({x}_{2}^{2}+1)=2{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{-1} & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nEvaluating $f$ and its derivative at $x=a=[\\begin{aligned}e \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],$ we have\n\n$$\nf(a)=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,{f}^{′}(a)=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-1} & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe linear approximation of $f$ at $x=a$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)≈f(a)+{f}^{′}(a)(x-a).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $f(a),$ ${f}^{′}(a),$ and $a$ in the equation above, we obtain\n\n$$\nf(x)≈[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-1} & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}](x-[\\begin{aligned}e \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the sum of the missing values is\n\n$$\n0+{e}^{-1}+(-2)={e}^{-1}-2.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186363642 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6a818e04-786a-56b6-90cf-dcb573ccfa64" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Derivative of a Vector Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "da23fd82-eeba-5726-977e-d84d081786c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}xy & 2x \\\\ 2(x-y) & -2(x-y)\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363644} {:answer/id #uuid "15d312ba-0b0d-5fd9-a675-24172c80b279" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2xy & {x}^{2} \\\\ 2(x-y) & -2(x-y)\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363645} {:answer/id #uuid "db47963d-1476-5bc4-a619-a48ea073c291" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}xy & 2x \\\\ x-y & y-x\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363646} {:answer/id #uuid "799582e5-f8ef-5727-9064-262ea9736abc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}xy & {x}^{2} \\\\ x-y & -(x-y)\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363647} {:answer/id #uuid "b068e577-95a8-53f4-b642-f15686168a0d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2xy & {x}^{2}y \\\\ -2(x-y) & 2(x-y)\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363648}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "15d312ba-0b0d-5fd9-a675-24172c80b279" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2xy & {x}^{2} \\\\ 2(x-y) & -2(x-y)\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363645} :answer-field/id #uuid "9877b7f3-ce64-54d5-b1a4-46b897ffabda" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363643}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "506e4392-8367-5c22-bb2c-6ffe4b882c6f" :question/math-academy-id "q-163097" :question/problem "For the transformation $f:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2},$ defined as\n\n$$\nf(x)=[\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}y \\\\ (x-y)^{2}\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\ncalculate ${f}^{′}(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose a transformation $f:{R}^{n}\\to {R}^{m}$ is defined by \n\n$$\nf:[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}{f}_{1}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}) \\\\ {f}_{2}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}) \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {f}_{m}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n})\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere ${f}_{1},{f}_{2},…,{f}_{m}$ are scalar functions with $n$ variables. If $f$ is differentiable at $x,$ then the total derivative of $f$ at $x,$ denoted ${f}^{′}(x),$ is given by the $m\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{n}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have the following:\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂x} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂y} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂x} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂y}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}y)=2xy,\\, & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}y)={x}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}((x-y)^{2})=2(x-y),\\, & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}((x-y)^{2})=-2(x-y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}2xy & {x}^{2} \\\\ 2(x-y) & -2(x-y)\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186363649 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6a818e04-786a-56b6-90cf-dcb573ccfa64" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Derivative of a Vector Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "443b6a1c-a9be-589e-83c0-8a1140e70862" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{y} & -\\frac{x}{{y}^{2}} \\\\ {e}^{x-y} & -{e}^{x-y}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363651} {:answer/id #uuid "d6f559c7-2497-5d3b-916b-fa64f3555eab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{y} & \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}} \\\\ {e}^{x-y} & -{e}^{x-y}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363652} {:answer/id #uuid "03c1fe89-d25c-5902-a4f8-bca8a98a4001" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{y} & {e}^{x-y} \\\\ -\\frac{x}{{y}^{2}} & -{e}^{x-y}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363653} {:answer/id #uuid "5fa2ce42-b90b-54f1-a3a2-eb4d781ac2ac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{x}{{y}^{2}} & \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}} \\\\ -y{e}^{x-y} & x{e}^{x-y}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363654} {:answer/id #uuid "76f573a1-7368-5da8-9b16-1b6705a1177c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{y} & \\frac{x}{{y}^{2}} \\\\ -{e}^{x-y} & {e}^{x-y}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363655}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "443b6a1c-a9be-589e-83c0-8a1140e70862" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{y} & -\\frac{x}{{y}^{2}} \\\\ {e}^{x-y} & -{e}^{x-y}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363651} :answer-field/id #uuid "d9eec273-47be-5315-9595-b7b23e1a3761" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363650}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c081a603-401b-56e2-8aa2-884420bee150" :question/math-academy-id "q-163099" :question/problem "For the transformation $f:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2},$ defined as\n\n$$\nf(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{y} \\\\ {e}^{x-y}\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\ncalculate ${f}^{′}(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose a transformation $f:{R}^{n}\\to {R}^{m}$ is defined by \n\n$$\nf:[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}{f}_{1}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}) \\\\ {f}_{2}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}) \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {f}_{m}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n})\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere ${f}_{1},{f}_{2},…,{f}_{m}$ are scalar functions with $n$ variables. If $f$ is differentiable at $x,$ then the total derivative of $f$ at $x,$ denoted ${f}^{′}(x),$ is given by the $m\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{n}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have the following:\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂x} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂y} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂x} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂y}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{x}{y})=\\frac{1}{y},\\, & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\frac{x}{y})=-\\frac{x}{{y}^{2}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({e}^{x-y})={e}^{x-y},\\, & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({e}^{x-y})=-{e}^{x-y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{y} & -\\frac{x}{{y}^{2}} \\\\ {e}^{x-y} & -{e}^{x-y}\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186363656 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6a818e04-786a-56b6-90cf-dcb573ccfa64" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Derivative of a Vector Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "83182517-8b01-5171-8594-d606b7e675e4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{y} & \\frac{y}{{x}^{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{y} & \\frac{1}{y}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363658} {:answer/id #uuid "793e6231-06fb-5b12-a92b-baa5ff9cb6f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{y} & \\frac{1}{x} \\\\ \\frac{y}{{x}^{2}} & \\frac{1}{y}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363659} {:answer/id #uuid "bbf2fde9-86b8-5e2b-bfac-54d168de5a93" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{x} & \\frac{1}{y} \\\\ \\frac{y}{{x}^{2}} & -\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363660} {:answer/id #uuid "4b0777b6-0f74-5d69-a4a3-2eb91257bb1b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{x} & \\frac{y}{{x}^{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{y} & \\frac{1}{x}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363661} {:answer/id #uuid "85394a8e-b189-5971-8c82-f628889e6c9c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{x} & \\frac{1}{y} \\\\ -\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}} & \\frac{1}{x}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363662}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "85394a8e-b189-5971-8c82-f628889e6c9c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{x} & \\frac{1}{y} \\\\ -\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}} & \\frac{1}{x}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363662} :answer-field/id #uuid "62c2b387-eeda-5d3f-b04a-943e86d1f6f6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363657}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6490b2e2-ebe2-52cf-9741-542b7f4cc483" :question/math-academy-id "q-163110" :question/problem "For the transformation $f:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2},$ defined as\n\n$$\nf(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xy) \\\\ \\frac{y}{x}\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\ncalculate ${f}^{′}(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose a transformation $f:{R}^{n}\\to {R}^{m}$ is defined by \n\n$$\nf:[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}{f}_{1}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}) \\\\ {f}_{2}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}) \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {f}_{m}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n})\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere ${f}_{1},{f}_{2},…,{f}_{m}$ are scalar functions with $n$ variables. If $f$ is differentiable at $x,$ then the total derivative of $f$ at $x,$ denoted ${f}^{′}(x),$ is given by the $m\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{n}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have the following:\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂x} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂y} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂x} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂y}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xy))=\\frac{1}{x},\\, & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xy))=\\frac{1}{y} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{y}{x})=-\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}},\\, & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\frac{y}{x})=\\frac{1}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{x} & \\frac{1}{y} \\\\ -\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}} & \\frac{1}{x}\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186363663 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6a818e04-786a-56b6-90cf-dcb573ccfa64" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Derivative of a Vector Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c68bfb0e-1744-5182-8e2b-0c71a77673f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x+2y,\\,$ $y,\\,$ and $\\frac{1}{x}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363665} {:answer/id #uuid "7fa59c9f-3c3c-5a2a-9b74-e31cc3bf2428" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x,\\,$ $y,\\,$ and $\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363666} {:answer/id #uuid "f534e1c1-3b85-5db9-8f01-2716b9f0712f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x+2y,\\,$ $x,\\,$ and $\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363667} {:answer/id #uuid "9c6c0c9d-0d28-50cf-bdad-07b26be6ce9e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x,\\,$ $x,\\,$ and $\\frac{1}{x}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363668} {:answer/id #uuid "5e62682b-140d-5e73-86b7-1f637bb63bb0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x+2y,\\,$ $x,\\,$ and $\\frac{1}{x}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363669}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5e62682b-140d-5e73-86b7-1f637bb63bb0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x+2y,\\,$ $x,\\,$ and $\\frac{1}{x}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363669} :answer-field/id #uuid "b9e5c214-0d67-5be0-98ea-63aedcf515da" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363664}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "38207a04-818a-52aa-b0a5-f930b6a5f009" :question/math-academy-id "q-163112" :question/problem "For the transformation $f:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{3},$ defined as\n\n$$\nf(x)=[\\begin{aligned}xy+{y}^{2} \\\\ xy \\\\ y+\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nthe total derivative ${f}^{′}$ is given by \n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}y &  \\\\ y &  \\\\  & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFrom top to bottom, what are the missing entries?" :question/worked-solution "Suppose a transformation $f:{R}^{n}\\to {R}^{m}$ is defined by \n\n$$\nf:[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}{f}_{1}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}) \\\\ {f}_{2}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}) \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {f}_{m}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n})\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere ${f}_{1},{f}_{2},…,{f}_{m}$ are scalar functions with $n$ variables. If $f$ is differentiable at $x,$ then the total derivative of $f$ at $x,$ denoted ${f}^{′}(x),$ is given by the $m\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{n}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have the following:\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂x} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂y} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂x} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂y} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{3}}{∂x} & \\frac{∂{f}_{3}}{∂y}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(xy+{y}^{2})=y,\\, & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(xy+{y}^{2})=x+2y, \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(xy)=y,\\, & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(xy)=x, \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{3}}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(y+\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{x},\\, & \\frac{∂{f}_{3}}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(y+\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}y & x+2y \\\\ y & x \\\\ \\frac{1}{x} & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThus, the missing entries are $x+2y,\\,$ $x,\\,$ and $\\frac{1}{x}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186363670 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9f09fc28-bdce-554f-98f5-019d34542a13" :knowledge-point/title "Finding an Affine Approximation of a Vector Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4a10e0f4-1a7b-50a9-9e1b-38baafb08f71" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1-2\\sqrt{\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363672} {:answer/id #uuid "bd51a913-c963-5cc4-a1d8-91253bb86614" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1+2\\sqrt{\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363673} {:answer/id #uuid "07108066-8631-5397-9f80-eea0dd04411f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-2\\sqrt{\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363674} {:answer/id #uuid "f12f81d2-9695-52f7-b33b-33a5187f716b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363675} {:answer/id #uuid "cfe768da-b224-5e62-8dfa-bf1e81cbe7a9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363676}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4a10e0f4-1a7b-50a9-9e1b-38baafb08f71" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1-2\\sqrt{\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363672} :answer-field/id #uuid "1284863d-77da-57f1-97a1-21b5ff0d735f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363671}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "444f8243-c558-52d9-9a66-13c87877fdd5" :question/math-academy-id "q-163158" :question/problem "Consider the transformation $f:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2},$ defined as\n\n$$\nf(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}_{1}^{2}) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡({x}_{2}^{2})\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf the linear approximation of $f$ at $a=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{\\pi } \\\\ \\sqrt{\\pi }\\end{aligned}]$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)≈[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ ∗\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}∗ & 0 \\\\ 0 & ∗\\end{aligned}](x-[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{\\pi } \\\\ \\sqrt{\\pi }\\end{aligned}]),\n$$\n\nwhat is the sum of the missing values?" :question/worked-solution "Suppose a transformation $f:{R}^{n}\\to {R}^{m}$ is defined by \n\n$$\nf:[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}{f}_{1}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}) \\\\ {f}_{2}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}) \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {f}_{m}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n})\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere ${f}_{1},{f}_{2},…,{f}_{m}$ are scalar functions with $n$ variables. If $f$ is differentiable at $x,$ then the total derivative of $f$ at $x,$ denoted ${f}^{′}(x),$ is given by the $m\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{n}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have the following:\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{2}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{2}}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{1}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{1}}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}_{1}^{2}))=2{x}_{1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡({x}_{1}^{2}),\\, & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{2}}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}_{1}^{2}))=0 \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{1}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{1}}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡({x}_{2}^{2}))=0,\\, & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{2}}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡({x}_{2}^{2}))=-2{x}_{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}_{2}^{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡({x}_{1}^{2}) & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2{x}_{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}_{2}^{2})\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nEvaluating $f$ and its derivative at $x=a=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{\\pi } \\\\ \\sqrt{\\pi }\\end{aligned}],$ we have\n\n$$\nf(a)=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,{f}^{′}(a)=[\\begin{aligned}-2\\sqrt{\\pi } & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe linear approximation of $f$ at $x=a$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)≈f(a)+{f}^{′}(a)(x-a).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $f(a),$ ${f}^{′}(a),$ and $a$ in the equation above, we obtain\n\n$$\nf(x)≈[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-2\\sqrt{\\pi } & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}](x-[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{\\pi } \\\\ \\sqrt{\\pi }\\end{aligned}]).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the sum of the missing values is\n\n$$\n-1+(-2\\sqrt{\\pi })+0=-1-2\\sqrt{\\pi }.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186363677 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9f09fc28-bdce-554f-98f5-019d34542a13" :knowledge-point/title "Finding an Affine Approximation of a Vector Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "541631ee-d4c3-5e4f-9d2b-663ecf332dc4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363679} {:answer/id #uuid "fe385b28-78db-5309-8cf0-ef4dcad524ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363680} {:answer/id #uuid "77cb299b-5820-566a-bad6-6dc14893c681" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363681} {:answer/id #uuid "e67e66f9-b48a-5876-8270-fc7a53987dd8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363682} {:answer/id #uuid "d879dd54-1587-59b7-abfb-d48e1226e034" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363683}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e67e66f9-b48a-5876-8270-fc7a53987dd8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363682} :answer-field/id #uuid "53ebf416-e445-554b-8e59-6c825e5853cc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363678}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "a9fb16b9-4450-5406-9622-d9c00f6085a1" :question/math-academy-id "q-163160" :question/problem "Consider the transformation $f:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2},$ defined as\n\n$$\nf(x)=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}^{-1} \\\\ {x}_{1}{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf the linear approximation of $f$ at $a=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}]$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)≈[\\begin{aligned}∗ \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}∗ & ∗ \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & 2\\end{aligned}](x-[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}]),\n$$\n\nwhat is the sum of the missing values?" :question/worked-solution "Suppose a transformation $f:{R}^{n}\\to {R}^{m}$ is defined by \n\n$$\nf:[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}{f}_{1}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}) \\\\ {f}_{2}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}) \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {f}_{m}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n})\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere ${f}_{1},{f}_{2},…,{f}_{m}$ are scalar functions with $n$ variables. If $f$ is differentiable at $x,$ then the total derivative of $f$ at $x,$ denoted ${f}^{′}(x),$ is given by the $m\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{n}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have the following:\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{2}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{2}}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{1}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{1}}({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}^{-1})=1,\\, & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{2}}({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}^{-1})=-{x}_{2}^{-2} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{1}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{1}}({x}_{1}{x}_{2})={x}_{2},\\, & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{2}}({x}_{1}{x}_{2})={x}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -{x}_{2}^{-2} \\\\ {x}_{2} & {x}_{1}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nEvaluating $f$ and its derivative at $x=a=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}],$ we have\n\n$$\nf(a)=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{f}^{′}(a)=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe linear approximation of $f$ at $x=a$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)≈f(a)+{f}^{′}(a)(x-a).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $f(a),$ ${f}^{′}(a),$ and $a$ in the equation above, we obtain\n\n$$\nf(x)≈[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & 2\\end{aligned}](x-[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}]).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the sum of the missing values is\n\n$$\n4+1+(-4)=1.\n$$"}]}
